    "schema_diff_summary": "load.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. At the start of load, when path.as_os_str() is empty, return LoadError::Io with ErrorKind::InvalidInput and the message The path is not a file. Keep the later not-a-file branch. Do not use ? for a missing path. Do not nest an if inside an if.  Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch open_load_file or sha256. The existing test load_of_a_directory_names_the_path stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test load_of_an_empty_path_names_the_path calls load on Path::new of an empty string. The error is LoadError::Io. The kind is InvalidInput. The display text is The path is not a file. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
